{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/40935-solar-non-lethality-charm-peach","id":40935,"title":"Solar Non-Lethality Charm (PEACH)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-01T23:13:49-08:00","id":40935,"title":"Solar Non-Lethality Charm (PEACH)","content":"So this is a bit of charm work to aid along those Martial Pacifists who don't feel like kung-fu. Because you should be able to make Kenshin using just melee charms, dammit. Or if you just want a duelist who doesn't kill his opponents all the time.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u><b>To Battle Under the Laurel</b></u></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1m; <b>Mins:</b> Melee 4, Essence 2;<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Combo-OK, Merged<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> To defeat without killing, to destroy without slaying. Such is the greatness of the Solars skill. So long as this charm is active, whenever a Solar reduces a foes to their final Incapacitated health level, that health level is always bashing, and no further levels of damage are done. This applies even to any poisons, diseases, environmental, or ongoing damage effects that originate from the Solar. Even bleeding wounds halt their flow as the opponent falls unconscious, and the there is no risk of infection even on the flithiest battlefields. Furthermore, they may recover from crippling wounds inflicted by an Exalt without any special measures, recovering at the normal rate for such an injury (if no time is given or the effect would be permanent, use mortal -4 health level healing times).<br /> <br /> Solars with this Charm and Compassion 3+ can choose to reflexively improve it at any time, transforming it into a costless Permanent effect. By suppressing their Compassion, they may deal damage as normal for a scene.<br /> <br /> Merged: Archery, Firearms, Martial Arts, Thrown<br /> <br /> Thoughts and comments?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":963,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/963-kylar","user":"Kylar","date":".  Minor edits and revised permanenet effect 01-02-2014, 03:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/963-kylar","name":"Kylar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar963_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T00:49:51-08:00","id":40966,"title":"","content":"I always just house rule that for essence users, unless the damage is 2x their total health levels in a single hit, death has to be a final coup de gras move after incap levels. So killing is an active decision and is almost never an accident. A charm to <i>not kill someone on accident</i> is silly, IMO.<br /> <br /> Unless its mortals. In which case an Exalt should not be fighting mortals if he doesn't want to accidentally level armies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1634-sareteni","name":"sareteni","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T01:10:37-08:00","id":40971,"title":"","content":"I disagree with sareteni. Being able to not kill something is a useful ability, not the least of which for the reason of now you never ever have to hold back against anyone.<br /> <br /> That said, that line about high-compassion solars is no good. Just make it cheap and step 10 and it will always be useful.<br /> <br /> Being able to just flat-out not apply damage she should of put on there would also be a neat ability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":673,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/673-requiem_jeer","user":"Requiem_Jeer","date":". 01-02-2014, 04:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/673-requiem_jeer","name":"Requiem_Jeer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar673_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T02:00:03-08:00","id":40987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sareteni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/40935-solar-non-lethality-charm-peach?p=40966#post40966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always just house rule that for essence users, unless the damage is 2x their total health levels in a single hit, death has to be a final coup de gras move after incap levels. So killing is an active decision and is almost never an accident. A charm to <i>not kill someone on accident</i> is silly, IMO.<br /> <br /> Unless its mortals. In which case an Exalt should not be fighting mortals if he doesn't want to accidentally level armies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rather silly. Of course. What was I thinking, playing a game where stabbing people with something sharp and pointy tends to have the possibility of killing them, baring supernatural skill and power. For rather liking the gritty feel and logic the logic that stabbing people or hitting them with a Toyota sized brick of of magical materials might kill them, and leave the players to deal with the consequences of their weapon choice. And of course, I'm UTTERLY silly for <i>thinking mortals matter.</i><br /> <br /> You house rule things so players don't have to worry about killing when they don't want to? That makes every death the result of cold blooded murder instead something that happens when lethal weapons come out? Bully for you, and if it works for your table more power to you. That said, the fact people probably die when lethal weapons come out fits the mood and theme's of Exalted quite nicely, and as such I don't see it as problem with the system. Unlike, say, accidentally leveling mortal armies. Which you can't actually do anyways, you need a specific Solar/Abyssal build, Essence 4 and the rather deliberate activation of charms to pull that off. Unless your referring to the mass combat system I politely ignore as having ever existed.<br /> <br /> So I'm sorry this isn't for you. Under your houserule, this charm is indeed meaningless. That said, for those of us that like weapons to be lethal, please do not insult us. I rather like the idea that if you want to be compassionate enough not to kill someone, if you want to be good enough to take someone alive using a lethal weapon, then you need to make an investment to get around an inherent nature of your weapon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Requiem_Jeer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/40935-solar-non-lethality-charm-peach?p=40971#post40971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, that line about high-compassion solars is no good. Just make it cheap and step 10 and it will always be useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its there more to get around the fact that, with this charm, you basically have to suppress your Compassion not to use it. Rather than force you to pay a cost one way or another, I just eliminated the more used cost, so you can save paying the costs for dramatically appropriate (and quite possibly Limit Inducing) moments.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Requiem_Jeer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/40935-solar-non-lethality-charm-peach?p=40971#post40971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being able to just flat-out not apply damage she should of put on there would also be a neat ability.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's more of a training Stunt, IMHO. I just don't really see what the utility of such a charm would be, not that it would be hard to make. &quot;The solar can, at-will, negate any amount damage or negative effects from any strike that they might make.&quot; Permanent effect, low mins, done. No idea what you would use it for, unless you just want a collateral damage dropper. Or something to screw up attack redirectors. Ok, few more uses than I thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/963-kylar","name":"Kylar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar963_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T02:57:39-08:00","id":40996,"title":"","content":"Ayep. Screwing up attack redirection, negating collateral damage, while no other uses for the ability come to mind, that's enough for most compassionate characters. Kind of a niche effect, which is why I usually place it on a artifact weapon as a special ability instead of picking up a charm.. And no, I wouldn't think that you would have to suppress compassion to not use it, except if your compassion would prevent you from raising your hand at all had you not possessed the charm. But I can see where you're coming from with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/673-requiem_jeer","name":"Requiem_Jeer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar673_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T03:37:26-08:00","id":41009,"title":"","content":"I made a charm quite similar once except I put it in War and let it upgrade to also apply to any unit the Solar led.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T07:22:00-08:00","id":41096,"title":"","content":"I'd say this is better than Subduing the Honored Foe (MoEPL p. 147) only because it doesn't cost anything to use. Otherwise it's noticeably inferior.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T07:38:37-08:00","id":41103,"title":"","content":"Such shouldn't be a charm <b>at all</b>. You don't want to kill? You don't kill. make it like this<br /> Bludgeoning damage incapacitated or killed? At your choice he's just down.<br /> Lethal/Agg damage incapacitated? At your choice he's just maimed instead of dead.<br /> <br /> At the most restrictive only experienced fighters (ability 3+) should have the option.<br /> <br /> That's it. The game already gives a similar rule but it's very clunky. All it needs to be is usable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T12:43:44-08:00","id":41250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kunoichi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/40935-solar-non-lethality-charm-peach?p=41009#post41009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I made a charm quite similar once except I put it in War and let it upgrade to also apply to any unit the Solar led.</div> </div> </div> </div>I considered War, but decided I'd rather it be freely available amongst the attack abilities, so as not to force heavy investment for non-Dawns. Playing a non-lethal character should not expensive!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/40935-solar-non-lethality-charm-peach?p=41096#post41096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say this is better than Subduing the Honored Foe (MoEPL p. 147) only because it doesn't cost anything to use. Otherwise it's noticeably inferior.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the minor effect of not doubling post soak damage (you are now imagining an E10 VBoS using Lunar with that charm) does balance things out a bit. And the much lower Mins of StHF. This was more balanced against the Crane Style in any case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/40935-solar-non-lethality-charm-peach?p=41103#post41103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Such shouldn't be a charm <b>at all</b>. You don't want to kill? You don't kill. make it like this<br /> Bludgeoning damage incapacitated or killed? At your choice he's just down.<br /> Lethal/Agg damage incapacitated? At your choice he's just maimed instead of dead.<br /> <br /> At the most restrictive only experienced fighters (ability 3+) should have the option.<br /> <br /> That's it. The game already gives a similar rule but it's very clunky. All it needs to be is usable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Called shots just convert down to bashing, and do nothing to stop the wrap around effect of damage. Not to mention there's bleeding, And disease. And crippling if you just hit them hard enough. Isn't being a mortal fun?<br /> <br /> Again, I honestly don't see the issue with making people pay for Batman/Kenshin level non-lethality. Weapons are inherently lethal, and this is a price you pay for better armor penetration. Its fairly potenet character statment, and quite neatly falls into &quot;their just that good&quot; aspect of Solar charms.<br /> <br /> <br /> Minor edits to the charm and revised permanent effect done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/963-kylar","name":"Kylar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar963_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T20:37:58-08:00","id":41484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kylar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/40935-solar-non-lethality-charm-peach?p=41250#post41250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Called shots just convert down to bashing, and do nothing to stop the wrap around effect of damage. Not to mention there's bleeding, And disease. And crippling if you just hit them hard enough. Isn't being a mortal fun?<br /> <br /> Again, I honestly don't see the issue with making people pay for Batman/Kenshin level non-lethality. Weapons are inherently lethal, and this is a price you pay for better armor penetration. Its fairly potenet character statment, and quite neatly falls into &quot;their just that good&quot; aspect of Solar charms.<br /> <br /> <br /> Minor edits to the charm and revised permanent effect done.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not talking about called shots, though the rules I refer to are over there as well. Problem is they both inflict the external penalty and have to be declared before the attack, which is very clunky.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T21:49:55-08:00","id":41511,"title":"","content":"I support the idea of this charm, though I think the charm itself needs to be <i>more</i>, especially for melee 4 essence 2 (right now it feels like a medicine charm imo, because it's most notable difference will be for poisons and diseases).<br /> <br /> Though this goes in the same vain as the Lunar charm, I'd suggest something like changing the cost to 1+ motes, where every mote beyond the first can convert a success (i.e. one of the ones that won't deal damage) into an automatic distinguishing feature, potentially like small mutations - physical damage creates scars that act like marks or sigils that point out criminals, diseases create birthmarks or change eye or hair color or maybe even grow tumors. (this can be really useful in cases where a solar sets fire to a building full of criminals, each one of them gets marked with a Burning Eye sigil representing guilt instead of being burned to death, or a specific variant of a disease marks anyone who comes into contact with the carrier to help with quarantine)<br /> <br /> Though again the disease/environment effects seem to me like they'd belong in Medicine.<br /> <br /> Although....<br /> <br /> I just realized that this is exactly like one of those ayssal cages - when used for torture you can go all out and make sure your victim lives and recovers in time for more excruciating pain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}